        page["route"] = "/doc/api/dvalue-set/"
        page["title"] = "DValue::set"
        page["content"] = "`dval_set(value, source)` replaces the target content. It mutates `value` and returns that same identity. All workspace aliases observe the mutation. Assigning the result back remains valid.\n\nA custom export or C++ boundary copies BRRB. Identity does not cross that boundary.\n\nCapy does not accept a C++ pointer or `StringMap` overload. Use `dval(...)` to create the source value.\n\n## C++ API\n\n`DValue::set()` changes the object in place. C++ overloads accept a string, pointer, f64, `DValue`, or `StringMap`.\n"
        page["returns"] = "replacement `dval` in Capy. C++ changes the receiver and returns nothing"
        page["example_error"] = "expected contiguous :example cpp render"
